[TEXT] **Breakthrough!** Router6 has an **nft FORWARD chain** that drops all transit traffic entering from eth2 (the r6_r3 inter-site backbone link). The counters show 44 packets already dropped. The rules:

1. **ACCEPT** only: TCP/80, src 172.16.10.0/24, dst 172.18.51.1 (one narrow exception)
2. **DROP** all TCP from eth2
3. **DROP** all UDP from eth2
4. **DROP** everything else from eth2 (catch-all with confirmed drop count)

This explains everything: router6 can ping pc15 because that traffic is **locally generated** (not forwarded through the FORWARD chain). But any transit traffic from router3 → Location C entering eth2 is completely blocked. IP forwarding is enabled (=1), so the block is purely the ACL.

This is the fault-family fingerprint for `acl-skill`. Phase 5 follows.

